// ============================================================
// Executed Book (L4) — the same trades behind a filtered mapping
// ============================================================
// Structurally identical to trading::Trade. The difference is entirely in the mapping:
// this class is bound to TRADE through a store filter, so it only ever sees the executed
// rows. That makes it a third invariance, independent of L2's and L4's union:
//
//   ExecutedTrade.all()  ==  Trade.all()->filter(t | $t.status == 'EXECUTED')
//
// One applies the predicate in the MAPPING, the other in the QUERY. Neither needs an
// oracle to know they must agree.
###Pure
Class trading::ExecutedTrade
{
    tradeId: String[1];
    tradeDate: StrictDate[1];
    quantity: Float[1];
    price: Float[1];
    notional: Float[1];
    side: trading::Side[1];
    status: String[1];
    currency: String[1];
}
